      <h2>The Money Transfer Problem</h2>
      <p>Moving money to Spain the traditional way is expensive. Your UK or US bank charges:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Transfer fee: €15-40</li>
        <li>Poor exchange rate (2-4% worse than mid-market): €50-150 hidden cost</li>
        <li>Receiving bank fee: €5-15</li>
        <li><strong>Total per €5,000 transfer: €70-205</strong></li>
      </ul>

      <p>A better option: Wise charges €5-15 per transfer with mid-market rates. On €5,000, you save €50-190 per transfer. Over a year of monthly transfers: <strong>€600-2,280 saved</strong>.</p>

      <h2>Wise (Formerly TransferWise)</h2>

      <h3>Why Wise Is Best for Regular Transfers</h3>
      <p>Wise specializes in international money transfers. They offer:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Real mid-market exchange rate:</strong> No markup (or 0.5-1% at most)</li>
        <li><strong>Low fees:</strong> €2-8 typically, based on amount and currency pair</li>
        <li><strong>Fast delivery:</strong> 1-3 business days, often faster</li>
        <li><strong>Multi-currency account:</strong> Hold euros, GBP, USD in one account; convert anytime</li>
        <li><strong>Mobile app:</strong> Easy tracking and frequent transfers</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>How Wise Works</h3>
      <ol style="list-style: decimal; padding-left: 1.75rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        <li>Create Wise account (online, few minutes)</li>
        <li>Verify identity and funding source</li>
        <li>Initiate transfer, specify amount and destination</li>
        <li>See exact fee and exchange rate before confirming</li>
        <li>Wise sends euros to your Spanish bank account</li>
        <li>Track delivery via app</li>
      </ol>

      <h3>Wise for Different Amounts</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Under €1,000:</strong> Fee roughly €2-3, rate excellent</li>
        <li><strong>€1,000-€10,000:</strong> Fee €3-8, best value</li>
        <li><strong>Over €10,000:</strong> Consider multi-currency account for regular transfers</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Wise Multi-Currency Account</h3>
      <p>If transferring regularly, open a Wise account with euro balance. Advantages:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Receive salary in USD/GBP, convert to EUR at your own rate</li>
        <li>Use euro debit card for Spanish purchases (no foreign fee)</li>
        <li>No monthly fee for account itself</li>
        <li>Lower transfer fees (€1-3) when using existing euro balance</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="msv__cta-mid">
        <h3>Need a Spanish Bank Account?</h3>
        <p>Once you have a Spanish address and NIE, open a local bank account (CaixaBank, Santander, etc.). Transfers land directly in your Spanish account from Wise.</p>
        <a href="/blog-opening-bank-account-spain-foreigner.html" style="color: var(--red); font-weight: 600;">Learn how to open a Spanish bank account →</a>
      </div>

      <h2>Revolut: Good for Small Transfers & Spending</h2>

      <h3>What Is Revolut?</h3>
      <p>Revolut is a mobile banking app offering:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Money transfers to Spain (€0.99-2 fee for small amounts)</li>
        <li>Multi-currency account (hold euros, spend anywhere)</li>
        <li>Debit card (free ATM withdrawals in Spain)</li>
        <li>Currency exchange at mid-market rates</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Revolut vs Wise</h3>
      <p><strong>Wise:</strong> Better for large transfers and regular payments home.</p>
      <p><strong>Revolut:</strong> Better for small transfers, spending in Spain, ATM access.</p>

      <h3>Revolut Costs</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Transfer to Spain: Free (standard) or €2 (instant)</li>
        <li>No ATM fees in Spain (up to limit)</li>
        <li>Currency conversion: Mid-market rate</li>
        <li>Premium plan: €4.99/month (better ATM limits, insurance)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Other Options</h2>

      <h3>SEPA Transfers (EU Banks Only)</h3>
      <p>If your home bank is in the EU (UK included until reciprocal agreements end), SEPA transfers are free and fast:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Fee:</strong> €0 (free)</li>
        <li><strong>Exchange rate:</strong> N/A (already in euros or you convert at bank rate)</li>
        <li><strong>Speed:</strong> 1-2 business days</li>
        <li><strong>Best for:</strong> Sending euros from EU accounts</li>
      </ul>

      <p>Check if your home bank offers SEPA transfers. If so, this is free and reliable, though not better exchange rates than Wise.</p>

      <h3>OFX (Now Remitly)</h3>
      <p>International money transfer service:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Fee:</strong> €3-5 typically</li>
        <li><strong>Exchange rate:</strong> Good but not as good as Wise</li>
        <li><strong>Speed:</strong> 1-3 days</li>
        <li><strong>Best for:</strong> US to Spain transfers, decent middle option</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>CurrencyFair</h3>
      <p>Peer-to-peer currency exchange:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Fee:</strong> €1-3</li>
        <li><strong>Exchange rate:</strong> Excellent (peer rates)</li>
        <li><strong>Speed:</strong> 1-3 days</li>
        <li><strong>Best for:</strong> Large amounts, competitive rates</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Traditional Bank SWIFT Transfers</h3>
      <p>Last resort—expensive and slow:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Fee:</strong> €30-50</li>
        <li><strong>Exchange rate:</strong> Poor (2-4% markup)</li>
        <li><strong>Speed:</strong> 3-5 business days</li>
        <li><strong>Only use if:</strong> No other option available</li>
      </ul>

