      <h2>Large Transfers: Buying Property or Moving Savings</h2>

      <h3>Transferring €100,000+ to Spain</h3>
      <p>For major amounts (property purchase, investment, relocation), savings are even larger:</p>

      <h3>Bank Cost: €100,000</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Transfer fee: €40-50</li>
        <li>Exchange loss (2.5%): €2,500</li>
        <li><strong>Total: €2,540-2,550</strong></li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Wise Cost: €100,000</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Transfer fee: €10-20</li>
        <li>Exchange loss (0.5%): €500</li>
        <li><strong>Total: €510-520</strong></li>
      </ul>

      <p><strong>Savings: €2,000-2,040 on a single large transfer.</strong></p>

      <h3>Tips for Large Transfers</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Split into multiple transfers if individual limits apply (Wise: no limit)</li>
        <li>Check exchange rates—don't send on days when rates are unfavorable</li>
        <li>Schedule transfer for mid-week (better rates than weekends)</li>
        <li>Use Wise's rate guarantee feature (hold rate for 48 hours)</li>
        <li>For property, coordinate timing with closing date</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Setting Up Regular Monthly Transfers</h2>

      <h3>Best Practice for Living Expenses</h3>
      <p>Many expats receive income abroad and transfer monthly to Spain. Best approach:</p>
      <ol style="list-style: decimal; padding-left: 1.75rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        <li>Open Wise multi-currency account</li>
        <li>Receive salary in home currency (USD, GBP, etc.)</li>
        <li>Hold in Wise account; convert to EUR when needed</li>
        <li>Transfer EUR to Spanish bank account monthly</li>
        <li>Set up recurring transfer for automation</li>
      </ol>

      <h3>Automation Options</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Wise:</strong> Set scheduled recurring transfers</li>
        <li><strong>Home bank:</strong> Schedule SEPA transfer if available</li>
        <li><strong>Manual:</strong> Transfer as needed if amounts vary</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>FAQs: Sending Money to Spain</h2>
      <div class="msv__faq">
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-question">What's the cheapest way to send money to Spain?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">Wise (formerly TransferWise) offers the best mid-market exchange rates with low fees (typically 0.5-2%). For regular transfers, it beats traditional banks by €20-50+ per transaction. Revolut is also competitive for smaller amounts.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-question">How long does it take to transfer money to Spain?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">SEPA transfers (EU banks): 1-2 business days, free. Wise: 1-3 business days depending on method, small fee. Traditional bank SWIFT transfers: 3-5 business days, expensive. Fastest: Revolut or Wise (same-day with premium options).</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-question">What is SEPA and how much does it cost?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">SEPA (Single Euro Payments Area) is a free system for transfers between EU banks. No fee, 1-2 day delivery. Available from most UK and EU banks. Ideal for regular monthly transfers. Use this if your home bank supports SEPA.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-question">Should I use a multi-currency account like Wise or Revolut?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">Yes, if you regularly transfer to Spain or manage multi-currency income. Hold euros, receive salary in USD/GBP and convert. Wise has better exchange rates; Revolut better for frequent spending/ATM use. Both save money vs traditional banks.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-question">What exchange rate should I expect when sending money?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">Mid-market rate is typically €1 = 1.10-1.15 USD or €1 = 0.85-0.87 GBP. Banks charge 2-4% markup. Wise charges 0.5-1.5% markup. Avoid sending money on weekends when rates are volatile.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-question">How much do bank fees add up when sending money?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">Traditional bank: €15-40 per transfer + bad exchange rates (€50-150 hidden loss). Wise: €2-5 per transfer + fair rate (minimal loss). Transferring €5,000: Bank costs €65-190 total; Wise costs €10-35. Over a year: Bank €2,000+ vs Wise €300.</div>
        </div>
